{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west","id":805109,"title":"A little question about Vampiric Buddhism in the West","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T03:08:02-08:00","id":805109,"title":"A little question about Vampiric Buddhism in the West","content":"I know that the title seems strange, but bear with me. Just before going to sleep yesterday, I suddenly thought : &quot;What would I become/do if I were to be Embraced ?&quot;. It's a strange question, and the strangest part was possibly the answer that I got : being mostly atheistic-agnostic in life, but with some interest in Buddhism and animist religions/faith, I was left with some serious questioning, especially for character concepts. Some years ago, I would have probably envisioned myself going toward the Carthians as an obvious choice, but as time passed, I've grown disillusioned with human parties and politics, so I've now a hard time seeing me joining any Covenant (the two &quot;political&quot; because I've lost faith in Politic, the two &quot;Faithful&quot; because I don't believe in God and I don't like the idea of strict &quot;churches&quot;/&quot;worship cults&quot;, and the mystical Ordo Dracul, while very attractive, would probably be abhorrent for me in the early Requiem).<br /> <br /> But I still believe that people Embraced need some semblance of &quot;solace&quot;, or at least something to rely upon, and I think that people like myself could turn toward whatever a &quot;proto-faith&quot; they had in their life. the problem is : what would be Vampiric Buddhism ? Especially here in the West ? As of today, there is many, if not temples, at least place of prayers for this religion in most Western Countries but I've no knowledge of Buddhism being portrayed in the WofD and the CofD; the other main faiths in the West (Judaism and the various branches of Islam), I've some knowledge of how they are portrayed from the basic Lancea et Sanctum, and anyway, being all abrahamic faiths, I could see how to tweak the Lancea the right way to have true Covenants specifically for the Judaism and Islam. But Buddhism resting on very different basis, with even less unity between its sects than in other great religions, I really can't begin to know from where to work on it.<br /> <br /> As a bonus question : would a neonate as I could see myself being could feasibly try to take control or at least ingrain himself/herself into the Bouddhist community of his town ? After all, it often seems to be a part of the population mostly left alone by the western Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 01-13-2016, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:59:16-08:00","id":805181,"title":"","content":"Officially, Buddhism has shown up in two books - the first was incorporated as part of the Ordo Dracul methodology as a way of achieving Transcendance. The second was as its own covenant in Tibet led by the Naga King, the vampire equivalent of the Dalai Lama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T06:01:52-08:00","id":805182,"title":"","content":"Really ? I suppose that the first is in the Ordo Dracul rulebook ? But the second, I've no idea where to find him !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:06:59-08:00","id":805655,"title":"","content":"I believe there's an Ordo Dracul-esque Covenant of Buddhist Monks that were inspired by Dracula's <i>Rites of the Dragon in </i>Hong Kong as well? They're in the 2e core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T18:41:29-08:00","id":805673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=805181#post805181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially, Buddhism has shown up in two books - the first was incorporated as part of the Ordo Dracul methodology as a way of achieving Transcendance. The second was as its own covenant in Tibet led by the Naga King, the vampire equivalent of the Dalai Lama.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Tibet, actually; Thailand. The Naga King was the ruler of the Kindred in the Sukhothai Kingdom, a Nosferatu representing himself as a sort of demon within the framework of the pre-Buddhist, Hinduism-influenced folk religion of the Thai people. He was converted to Buddhism after encountering an itinerant holy woman known only as the &quot;Mae Ji&quot; (more typical current transliteration would be Maechi). The Mae Ji seems to have been the originator of a system of beliefs and practices resembling some of the teachings of the Ordo Dracul, and these teachings have been passed down and perhaps refined by Buddhist vampires in Thailand ever since.<br /> <br /> It's not clear if the sort of Kindred Buddhism practiced in Thailand has spread very far outside of Thai lands. Assuming that the fortunes of the Thai Kindred followed those of their mortal relations, their culture and institutions may have made some inroads into what are now Burma and Cambodia. The Mae Ji herself is said to have ultimately gone away to the west, leaving open the possibility that he teachings reached other kindred, and possibly even influenced the development of the Ordo Dracul in Europe.<br /> <br /> This is all from <i>Ancient Mysteries</i>, by the way.<br /> <br /> In the Beijing chapter of the 2nd edition book, it's apparent that the vampires of China have their on philosophical can mystical schools that bear some resemblance to the Ordo Dracul, and have been influenced by the <i>Rites of the Dragon</i> since it became available in China. In Beijing itself, these schools are the Way of the Dragon and the Dragon's Path, but there may be other, similar institutions elsewhere in China. Like mortal Chinese Philosophy and Religion, I suspect that these groups would draw upon a variety of influences, including China's various schools of Buddhism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:16:58-08:00","id":805943,"title":"","content":"So, in both cases the Ordo Dracul and the Buddhism are somewhat tied ? Interesting. Then I guess that tweaking the Ordo somewhat would allow for what I was seeking. Obviously, in the West, I think that Buddhism would be more of simply another mysticism to the Ordo ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:09:12-08:00","id":805992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=805943#post805943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in both cases the Ordo Dracul and the Buddhism are somewhat tied ? Interesting. Then I guess that tweaking the Ordo somewhat would allow for what I was seeking. Obviously, in the West, I think that Buddhism would be more of simply another mysticism to the Ordo ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Basically? The Ordo Dracul is the Transcendence covenant, which is where (for the standard western covenants) any kind of ascension, transformation, or even Golconda seeking tends to end up. Seeking out a state of Nirvana is thematically close to that idea of Transcendence that its inevitable that the Ordo Dracul would absorb at least some of the practices. <br /> <br /> There's some question on how, of if, buddhist vampires would develop other advantages along with the Coils. Blood alchemy (key for the development of Scales), despite everything, seems to be the main Modus Operandus of the Ordo Dracul, followed by geomancy (wyrm nests). In the past, you could justify buying up the Mind of the Unblinking Serpent style merits through buddhist style learning, but there's no equivalent in 2e. Even the Rites of the Impailed tend to be more scientific. So, do keep in mind that this isn't a perfect fit. And, if we go by the Ancient books, there is actually a kind of rivalry between the Ordo and the Naga, sparking over into violence. <br /> <br /> How all this manifests is going to be up to you to discuss with your ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=805673#post805673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not Tibet, actually; Thailand.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're probably right, I was going off memory. Though, I should point out that it was from Ancienty Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines together - the books are intertwined.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=805655#post805655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there's an Ordo Dracul-esque Covenant of Buddhist Monks that were inspired by Dracula's <i>Rites of the Dragon in </i>Hong Kong as well? They're in the 2e core.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. Forgot about them. It feels like they've got a Belial's Brood / Ordo Dracul split going on with them there, dark enlightenment versus control. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:04:56-08:00","id":807282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=805992#post805992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How all this manifests is going to be up to you to discuss with your ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm the ST with my friends ^^. Even if we don't get to play often... I should really seek out a group of players in my town.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, that's quite interesting, because from what I understand, Buddhist members of the Ordo Dracul could actually ascribe to a more metaphysical approach of the Coils than a scientifical one. It would, potentially, add a lot of infighting, or at least tensions within the Ordo then (without even counting the members of both the Lancea et Sanctum and the Circle being incensed by a Buddhist Kindred in the West). But I guess that it could be possible to advance throughout the Ordo with &quot;faith&quot; or dedication alone, if one manage to change his very mindset enough to manifest a Coil, no ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:24:24-08:00","id":807296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=807282#post807282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonetheless, that's quite interesting, because from what I understand, Buddhist members of the Ordo Dracul could actually ascribe to a more metaphysical approach of the Coils than a scientifical one. It would, potentially, add a lot of infighting, or at least tensions within the Ordo then (without even counting the members of both the Lancea et Sanctum and the Circle being incensed by a Buddhist Kindred in the West)</div> </div> </div> </div> I doubt the Circle would be particularly upset over the matter. They're pretty much vampire neo-pagans, and anything that sticks in the LetS craw is a good thing in their books. LetS might not like it, but that's because they don't like any religious rivals, not particularly because they're in the &quot;west.&quot; That implies that the Lance would be okay with Buddhist vampires in general - the LetS wants to convert all vampires across the world. Spread the Faith. <br /> <br /> Certainly, there'd be internal drama. Even if its just over arguing over different techniques. Or if the buddhist-themed vamps should even be considered part of the Ordo Dracul, or the equivalent of a heresy that's on the outs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I guess that it could be possible to advance throughout the Ordo with &quot;faith&quot; or dedication alone, if one manage to change his very mindset enough to manifest a Coil, no ? </div> </div> </div> Not at all. Developing Coils is still very much a very outgoing process, not just navel gazing. There's a lot of issues, such as working off karma, testing boundries, and its still about understanding yourself and the vampire condition; faith and dedication have nothing to do with it, unless you count faith and dedication to putting the work in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:10:44-08:00","id":807436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=805655#post805655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there's an Ordo Dracul-esque Covenant of Buddhist Monks that were inspired by Dracula's <i>Rites of the Dragon in </i>Hong Kong as well? They're in the 2e core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember them. Where in the core do they appear?<br /> <br /> In fact, in Ancient Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines it's suggested just the opposite. That Dracula learned about the Trascendence and the coils through the Sakadagami.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:44:14-08:00","id":807458,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't use Ancient Mysteries or Ancient Bloodlines as reliable sources in the 2nd Edition, though they're great inspiration in lieu of more information about what things were like in x or y place.<br /> <br /> They appear in the setting write-up for Beijing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:54:19-08:00","id":807538,"title":"","content":"Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:44:31-08:00","id":807688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=807296#post807296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. Developing Coils is still very much a very outgoing process, not just navel gazing. There's a lot of issues, such as working off karma, testing boundries, and its still about understanding yourself and the vampire condition; faith and dedication have nothing to do with it, unless you count faith and dedication to putting the work in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I meant, in fact, because for me, Buddhism actually require the Buddhist to act (at list for the Theravada and the early forms of Mahayana, perhaps a little less for the Vajrayana) because he can becomes an Arhant/Boddhistava only by working out, changing himself willfully, because there is no God/gods which will grant him the Illumination, meaning that to achieve his goals, a Buddhist must change his mindset by going against human nature (at least in theory). Plus, since Buddhism is/was supposed to be workable for every plane of existence (humans, beasts, wraith, demons, gods and a sixth I'm forgetting right now), I guess that actually experiencing what would be the correct path for an undead to be a Buddhist would require a lot of work, and science and knowledge would probably be a very important part of finding the proper way (and now that I think of it, it could be a potential plot hook : Buddhist masters of old had supposedly hidden Sutra to be found out later... but what if Buddha had had an undead Disciple who wrote Sutra from the specific lessons he had heard from the Master and had hidden them around the world ? The knowledge in there could be of interest for the Ordo... but it could also threaten it, should it be used to promote an &quot;heresy&quot; among the Dragons).<br /> <br /> In fact, more I think about how Buddhism and Vampirism can intermingle, the more I want to delve into all the possibilities.<br /> <br /> Damn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T06:50:54-08:00","id":807837,"title":"","content":"&quot;Faith Alone,&quot; while a popular Catholic stance, is actually a deviance from how the overwhelming majority of Abrahamic religions. However, when people say &quot;by faith&quot; that's generally the doctrine they mean. So, I kind of have a knee jerk reaction to it. Anyways, there's a fair amount of discussion about purely Buddhist vamps in the Ancient books. I highly recommend taking a look at those two sections in there if you get a chance to do it. Probably not worth the cost of the books for just this, but if you know a friend who will lend you the books for a bit during gaming night, I recommend you do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (humans, beasts, wraith, demons, gods and a sixth I'm forgetting right now), </div> </div> </div> EDIT - I was wrong. You've got deva, asura, and hellish beings. The asura and the hell kingdoms have both been called &quot;demons&quot; before, so maybe that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-13-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T07:38:43-08:00","id":807870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=807837#post807837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Faith Alone,&quot; while a popular Catholic stance, is actually a deviance from how the overwhelming majority of Abrahamic religions. However, when people say &quot;by faith&quot; that's generally the doctrine they mean. So, I kind of have a knee jerk reaction to it. Anyways, there's a fair amount of discussion about purely Buddhist vamps in the Ancient books. I highly recommend taking a look at those two sections in there if you get a chance to do it. Probably not worth the cost of the books for just this, but if you know a friend who will lend you the books for a bit during gaming night, I recommend you do it.<br /> <br /> EDIT - I was wrong. You've got deva, asura, and hellish beings. The asura and the hell kingdoms have both been called &quot;demons&quot; before, so maybe that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to find the books, at least to have some sort of idea of what exist(ed?) in the 1ed. It may takes some time to get my hands on it, though.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;worlds&quot; of Buddhism, I find interesting the fact that among the Three Inferiors (The Hellish Worlds, the worlds inhabited by the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preta\" target=\"_blank\">Preta</a> and the worlds inhabited by the animals), the second ones are described as being always hungry, living miserable existences, feeding being hurtful and difficult for them.<br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, I could see how to forge some sort of &quot;Buddha talked about the Kindred when he talked about the Preta !&quot;, perhaps more specifically a brood or bred of Nosferatu perhaps. Obviously, it would be a deviation of the Buddhism as it exists in our world, but in the CofD, I think it may works, couldn't it ?<br /> <br /> Edit : as for the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deva_%28Buddhism%29\" target=\"_blank\">Deva</a>... well they could be Daeva, being more able to fool humans into seeing them as living great lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 01-13-2016, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:51:50-08:00","id":808975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=807458#post807458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't use Ancient Mysteries or Ancient Bloodlines as reliable sources in the 2nd Edition, though they're great inspiration in lieu of more information about what things were like in x or y place.<br /> <br /> They appear in the setting write-up for Beijing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be so dismissive of first edition fluff. The 2e Vampire core is full of references to setting fluff introduced in first edition books. The Sanctified Mission in San Francisco first showed up in <i>Daeva: Kiss of the Succubus</i>, the art for the Lancea et Sanctum section clearly depicts a prominent Sanctified vampire whose name I've forgotten from a bunch of 1e fiction, and Rose has stated that the vampires depicted in the Clan writeups (with the exception of the Nosferatu) are characters appearing in the 1e Clanbooks.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are bound to be some contraditictions between the new fluff and the old fluff, but the old fluff was full of contradictions already. Feel free to use whatever sources you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:03:39-08:00","id":808993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=808975#post808975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't be so dismissive of first edition fluff. The 2e Vampire core is full of references to setting fluff introduced in first edition books. The Sanctified Mission in San Francisco first showed up in <i>Daeva: Kiss of the Succubus</i>, the art for the Lancea et Sanctum section clearly depicts a prominent Sanctified vampire whose name I've forgotten from a bunch of 1e fiction, and Rose has stated that the vampires depicted in the Clan writeups (with the exception of the Nosferatu) are characters appearing in the 1e Clanbooks.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are bound to be some contraditictions between the new fluff and the old fluff, but the old fluff was full of contradictions already. Feel free to use whatever sources you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Ancient Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines have massive contributed to the CofD timeline I've built and some of the best fluff WW wrote is in those books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:38:42-08:00","id":809040,"title":"","content":"I'm not dismissive of the fluff in the sense that I think it's bad. There's just stuff in the 2nd edition writing that contradicts it, which calls it all into question. Further, while a lot of it is really cool (I loved those books!) I think a lot of it is still constructed with the mentality that all the groups need to reflect the Five Covenants in modern nights, which is IMO a weakness of the material. Those are the reasons I suggest using it as inspiration rather than treating it as still default.<br /> <br /> Also I should clarify, when I said I wouldn't consider certain things &quot;canon&quot; it was <i>only </i>in reference to Ancient Mysteries and Bloodlines. Fluff occupies a certain level of abstraction anyway.<br /> <br /> I could point you to a number of other references to 1e concepts, but that's not really the point. I'm just hesitant to use resources which haven't gotten the 2e &quot;shine&quot; as-is. The Clanbooks are inspirational material anyway, and they're explicitly called out in the books. I often make material for my games inspired by the Covenant books, but I wouldn't necessarily use them as-is because of other points in the presentation of the Covenants which have changed as well, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 01-14-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:39:11-08:00","id":809201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=809040#post809040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not dismissive of the fluff in the sense that I think it's bad. There's just stuff in the 2nd edition writing that contradicts it, which calls it all into question. Further, while a lot of it is really cool (I loved those books!) I think a lot of it is still constructed with the mentality that all the groups need to reflect the Five Covenants in modern nights, which is IMO a weakness of the material. Those are the reasons I suggest using it as inspiration rather than treating it as still default.<br /> <br /> Also I should clarify, when I said I wouldn't consider certain things &quot;canon&quot; it was <i>only </i>in reference to Ancient Mysteries and Bloodlines. Fluff occupies a certain level of abstraction anyway.<br /> <br /> I could point you to a number of other references to 1e concepts, but that's not really the point. I'm just hesitant to use resources which haven't gotten the 2e &quot;shine&quot; as-is. The Clanbooks are inspirational material anyway, and they're explicitly called out in the books. I often make material for my games inspired by the Covenant books, but I wouldn't necessarily use them as-is because of other points in the presentation of the Covenants which have changed as well, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree wholeheartedly. Also, it's one thing to keep the truth vague, and another to assume that somehow the denizens of this fictional world are fully aware of our inability to know for sure. People, let alone vampires, love being opinionated. The fourth wall comes crumbling down when this kind of conviction in one's personal version of how things happened in the past, is solely reserved for the five clans and the five covenants. Everything else feels like it has been subjected to a clean-up crew's treatment, with nothing but loose ties in the form of bullet points at the point of an otherwise promising write-up.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I am misunderstood as a fan of how Masquerade did things in the mythos department. Personally, I can't imagine playing or ST'ing in VtM without assuming the entire Caine mythos is <i>fabricated</i>! But it's nice they have historian NPCs investing into the fiction, panicking over how their mythology <i>could</i> be true. That's the whole point of religion and politics after all, no? Where were the lovely Edimmu later on in the line? Out of all places, how no one in the world of chronicles of darkness simultaneously researched both them and the Strix? Oh, and where are the Strix experts in the fiction? Unless I'm missing something, there's a sort of pervasive inconsistency that although declining, hasn't completely died out. No, not the kind of inconsistency that makes things optional and easy for the ST to come up with original ideas. I'm talking about the kind of inconsistency that makes anything beyond the core awkward to co-exist with elements across the books.<br /> <br /> I think the clanbooks were impeccable, and clearly representative of the kind of writing that should be allowed to shine in 2e.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines are another perfect example. I'm all for choice, but it's kind of sad that players can't really relate and grow attached to bloodlines because of their absence from any other book published later on. The Khaibit and a few others are the obvious exception, but it would still be nice to see iconic characters and moments in history where certain bloodlines made a difference. Certain broods, or elder conclaves, or coteries, actually made a name for themselves and pushed the covenants into a tight, uncomfortable spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 01-14-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T06:08:25-08:00","id":809538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=809040#post809040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not dismissive of the fluff in the sense that I think it's bad. There's just stuff in the 2nd edition writing that contradicts it, which calls it all into question.</div> </div> </div> </div> While a lot of the earlier books have this issue, the later books, especially the clan books, were what actually inspired there to be the 2nd edition in the first place! The lore had changed too much from the early days to the latter that we needed to update the core book. The Ancient books tend to reflect more of 2e's mindset and history than 1e's.<br /> <br /> So, while the mechanics aren't great, the story is actually fairly up to date in terms of 2e. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Further, while a lot of it is really cool (I loved those books!) I think a lot of it is still constructed with the mentality that all the groups need to reflect the Five Covenants in modern nights, which is IMO a weakness of the material. </div> </div> </div> The core five covenants are archetypes. In fact, they're kind of reflections of clan-mindsets. The Invictus (and all similar covenants) reflect the Ventrue mindset taken to an extreme, the vampire noble houses. The Movement reflects the Daeva (passionate rebels - Bruja anyone?), the Ordo reflects Mehket (occultists), the Circle and Lance the Gangrel (wild-nature) and Nosferatu (empathy with the dead/damned, necropolis) respectively. So, naturally, you're going to see any other covenant as a reflection of the core seven once you include the demonic Brood (strix) and the killer VII. Because all the covenants are derived from the same universal vampire archetypes. <br /> <br /> There's a reason that the &quot;lost clans&quot; and &quot;broken covenants&quot; still look like the modern clans/covenants. Even the Child's Crusade became a reflection of a kid-infested Brood line, and the Legion of the Dead became mercinary assassins like certain other covenant based on the Aasimites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:17:35-08:00","id":809727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=809538#post809538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason that the &quot;lost clans&quot; and &quot;broken covenants&quot; still look like the modern clans/covenants. Even the Child's Crusade became a reflection of a kid-infested Brood line, and the Legion of the Dead became mercinary assassins like certain other covenant based on the Aasimites.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Broken Covenants <i>aren't </i>like the big Five though, which is what makes them interesting. The Legion of the Dead's closest analogue (and its ancestor) is the Legio Mortuum, and they're unique from the Five Covenants. The Gallow's Post is not like any of the Covenants in Modern Nights. The Weihan Cynn merely share an aesthetic with the Crones, but they're refreshingly distinct. The Children's Crusade as a 'covenant' does not align with any of the others, even if they become a chaotic enemy that resembles the Brood if you squint.<br /> <br /> The Ministry of Silence in Beijing does not feel the need to look like any of the Big Five. Neither do the Watchful Eyes in Berlin. The <i>zaibatsu </i>of Tokyo also aren't so easily pigeonholed, it's one of the best parts about the 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> I say all this to make the point that the Lost Covenants <i>don't </i>resemble the Big Five at all really, and it's one of the strengths of the new edition.<br /> <br /> As I recall, in the 1st edition, there was a certain obligation to represent the five as archetypes. I think they even had to. That's a weakness of some of the later products that couldn't really be helped. What I'm talking about doing is being strategic in what inspires you in the books. <i>Requiem for Regina </i>makes it clear that the Icarian Bloodline plays a big part in the politics of the time period among European Kindred, for example. I'd probably use them since they made it into the 2e material. There's mention of the different Creeds in <i>Regina </i>as well, though because it's from the Lancea's sorta iffy Covenant book, I'd look carefully at which ones to use (I probably wouldn't use the Dammitic Creed or the Iblic Creed for instance, because they actually are the perfect examples of victims of 1e's everything must be Big Five vibe.) but I'd certainly look at them to inspire. (I've used the rituals and shit in the Lancea et Sanctum book as inspiration for what Sanctified characters actually do.)<br /> <br /> To bring it back to the question of vampiric buddhism, the previously mentioned Beijing Covenants are not going to give you extensive writeups that describe what they do, but what IS said about them might serve as inspiration for how some vampires might internalize buddhism.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T19:23:45-08:00","id":810014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=809727#post809727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Broken Covenants <i>aren't </i>like the big Five though, which is what makes them interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, yes they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ministry of Silence in Beijing does not feel the need to look like any of the Big Five. Neither do the Watchful Eyes in Berlin. The <i>zaibatsu </i>of Tokyo also aren't so easily pigeonholed, it's one of the best parts about the 2nd edition. </div> </div> </div> I've actually talked to one of the developers about how I found them all to be comparable to the standard five.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I say all this to make the point that the Lost Covenants <i>don't </i>resemble the Big Five at all really, and it's one of the strengths of the new edition. </div> </div> </div> Agree to disagree. I draw lots of similarites. They're calling down the same archetypes, if you believe it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T19:56:11-08:00","id":810032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=810014#post810014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, yes they are.<br /> <br /> I've actually talked to one of the developers about how I found them all to be comparable to the standard five.<br /> <br /> Agree to disagree. I draw lots of similarites. They're calling down the same archetypes, if you believe it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same way Plato was the founder of Stalinism and Sparta the first national socialist state, I guess (in the sense of not really but maybe under a certain lens).<br /> <br /> Did a dev confirm that that's what they're going for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T22:48:38-08:00","id":810094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=810014#post810014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, yes they are.<br /> <br /> I've actually talked to one of the developers about how I found them all to be comparable to the standard five.<br /> <br /> Agree to disagree. I draw lots of similarites. They're calling down the same archetypes, if you believe it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then perhaps a better way to put it: They call down those same archetypes in a less transparent fashion. My chief beef with Ancient Mysteries, the book I'd go to bat for, is that it does so in a more transparent fashion. One of the best parts of the 2e writing has been that they've managed to evoke those same archetypes without making them identical to the Big Five. Props to them for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:27:55-08:00","id":811258,"title":"","content":"So, I managed to get my hands to Ancient Bloodline at my local store (in English), and I've some questions regarding the Naga King Bloodline, it appears that they Embrace those who are truly despicable, the worst of the worst. Is it somehow more shared by Buddhist Kindred, or is it really peculiar to this Nosferatu Bloodline ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T17:45:13-08:00","id":811413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=809040#post809040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not dismissive of the fluff in the sense that I think it's bad. There's just stuff in the 2nd edition writing that contradicts it, which calls it all into question.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about the second edition material contradiction first edition material (at least when it comes to specific people, places, organizations, and events) is that first edition material also contradicts first edition material. A lot. Occasionally in different sections of the same book. I doubt that this is entirely unintentional; the fact that the CoD is a tool box rather than a rigidly constructed setting means that there's really no reason not to include every cool, well-written idea that the writers can come up with, even if they don't quite jive with other, previously published cool ideas. In your own version of the setting you can pick and choose which pieces of fluff you like best, but I don't think at this point that anyone can say with any authority what's part of the world of <i>Requiem</i> and what's not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T00:31:16-08:00","id":811592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=811258#post811258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I managed to get my hands to Ancient Bloodline at my local store (in English), and I've some questions regarding the Naga King Bloodline, it appears that they Embrace those who are truly despicable, the worst of the worst. Is it somehow more shared by Buddhist Kindred, or is it really peculiar to this Nosferatu Bloodline ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I would guess this is a left over from Masquerade, Kindred of the East where vampires were souls sent back from the earlier mentioned versions of Hell with more worthy souls moving along the wheel of reincarnation. It doesn't have to be the norm for eastern vampires unless you want them to be, like in Masquerade, a totally different kind of vampire. In that version they weren't even embraced by another vampire. If you want a Buddhist vampire type or bloodline ( I recommend the later) than start by looking at the basic tenants of the religion and any myths that might accompany it, then just imagine how they might be based on CofD vampires. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T11:25:39-08:00","id":811966,"title":"","content":"Well, I have in mind three western bloodlines, but I don't know what's considered too much or too little for them in the 2ed. Basically, I would like one Bloodline for each great form of Buddhism, the Ashoka for the Theravada, the M\u0169\u0111en for Mahayana and the Mgoshubs Nagpo for Vajrayana. All founded by Western Vampire, so their takes and ties on Buddhism can be very twisted, even for Vampires.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T11:49:17-08:00","id":811984,"title":"","content":"Given how twisted the Lance is I think that would be par for the course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T11:54:24-08:00","id":811988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/805109-a-little-question-about-vampiric-buddhism-in-the-west?p=811966#post811966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I have in mind three western bloodlines, but I don't know what's considered too much or too little for them in the 2ed. Basically, I would like one Bloodline for each great form of Buddhism, the Ashoka for the Theravada, the M\u0169\u0111en for Mahayana and the Mgoshubs Nagpo for Vajrayana. All founded by Western Vampire, so their takes and ties on Buddhism can be very twisted, even for Vampires.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds interesting, though I just want to put the thought out there: Do they need to be Bloodlines, or could they simply be strains of thought/factions of Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T11:57:51-08:00","id":811992,"title":"","content":"Well, I see them being both, not all of them being the two, however, because they would have happened during the early Victorian era for the Ashoka (so they could have had a larger impact than just bloodline), but the M\u0169\u0111en were founded at the very end of the XIXth Century and the Mgoshubs Nagpo claim to be a Bloodline, but aren't yet (so they would be more of a strain of thought/small faction pretending to be a bloodline for the outsiders).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:16:12-08:00","id":812197,"title":"","content":"I think the pretending to be a bloodline bit is unnecessary, but all this sounds very cool. I'd love to hear more as you develop them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}